(D6: Discrepancy 6 - `Write <scalar variable> to <file>` SEGFAULTED. This
 is vox bug #40, which was recorded as fixed in 0.4.7 but still reproduced
 against the 0.4.7 binary: a Number, a Float and a Boolean variable all
 crashed, while a Text variable and a buffer were fine and a scalar LITERAL
 (Write 42 to output.) was already a parse error.
 **RESOLVED - fixed by vox #40 (0.4.8).** The variable form is now caught
 at compile time by the same class of guard that caught the literal, with
 a diagnostic naming the rewrite. No binary is produced and nothing
 crashes. (The caret points at the DECLARATION of the offending variable
 rather than at the Write statement.)
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/D6.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   error: Cannot write number count to a file; Write takes text, a buffer, or a format string. Render it as text: Write "{count}" to output.
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
   (exit status 139)
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
a number called count is 42.
open a file for writing called output at "vf_scratch/files/scalar.txt".
Write count to output.
Close output.
print "survived writing a Number to a file".
